+2.  **2D Hexagon Distance**: Calculate the distance from $(q_x, q_y)$ to the 2D hexagonal cross-section.
+    *   *Variant A (Approximation/Flat-topped)*: Used in [S2, unofficial]. This variant assumes a specific orientation where the hexagon is defined by linear inequalities.
